{"seq":18,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T02:28:52.156Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"4108f24fd15ba4379e10d95fcdee5b02dfce358b5421d40502ad2d15f8e82d6b","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina, here's the list labelled by account. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419 (open, per Moss's Coastal cheat sheet): `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length.\n- Gate 4 chassis pool validation during shift change: an ongoing friction point in the cheat sheet, with no ticket number given.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by DMF warehouse managers.\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. No ticket number in the notes.\n- Patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (Moss's 11/02 digest). No ticket number.\n\n**Worth checking before Kwame's review**\n- Moss's 11/02 digest also logs ticket #4419 as Kwame's port account's barge slip 7 schedule sync, under Puget Sound Operations, which is DMF's region. The cheat sheet puts #4419 on PHL. Someone should confirm which account it belongs to.\n- Your own public cutover recap note (Dec 2025) mentions ticket PD-8841, a PHL chassis pool hold issue on Gate 4B. I left it out because it isn't in Moss's notes or the Coastal channels. I can add it if you want.\n\nSources: #coastal-team, #coastal-random, and Moss's Coastal cheat sheet, 5/18 coverage check, 10/05 and 11/02 digests. I excluded the Pellow items (PD-4821, PD-4824, #8812) and the Saltmarsh and Pemberline Dock access items (PD-4827) because they don't match your account filter."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
